  </h2>
</mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif;" color="#000000">
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin-top: 2px !important;">
    DHS seeks data
  </h2>
</mj-text>
<mj-image
  border-radius="10px"
  padding="10px 12px"
  width="600px"
  src="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
  alt="DHS seeks data"
  href="https://www.presidentialsummary.com/"
/>
<mj-text padding="10px 12px" font-family="Roboto+Serif" color="#000000">
  <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>What’s happening? </strong>The US Department of Homeland Security (DHS) is <a href="https://edition.cnn.com/2026/03/11/politics/homeland-security-child-support-database-immigration" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none;
                border-bottom: 2px solid #4d3060;
                color: black;">seeking access to a child-support database</a> held by the US Department of Health and Human Services that contains employment data. It’s the latest in a series of attempts by the Trump administration to use data stored in various federal agencies to potentially find undocumented immigrants residing in the US.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>Background:</strong> This follows a pattern of inter-agency data grabs, such as last year's Internal Revenue Service sharing of taxpayer addresses with ICE for 47,000 suspected undocumented individuals. DHS has pursued similar access through memoranda of understanding after Elon Musk's DOGE eyed the same child support database.</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5"><strong>Criticism: </strong>Critics, including former officials and privacy advocates, warn that the proposal could violate federal law governing the use of such data. Former child support enforcement commissioner Vicki Turetsky said opening the database to immigration authorities could expose information about workers and undermine trust in a system designed to support families.</p>
</mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>

<mj-spacer height="10px" />
<mj-section
  background-color="#eff1f4"
